.TH EXPIRY-RADAR 1 "2026-09" "expiry-radar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
expiry-radar \- one inventory of everything that expires, ranked by blast radius
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B expiry-radar
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B expiry-radar
collects everything in an estate that has an expiry date \(em TLS certificates,
intermediate CAs, secrets, IAM keys, Vault leases, domains \(em into one report,
ranked by blast radius, so that the certificate on the payment path outranks the
one on a staging dashboard.
.PP
All sources are read-only. The project documentation carries the exact IAM
policy and Kubernetes RBAC Role required.
.PP
Partial failures are reported, never swallowed: if a source fails, the report is
still written, a warning goes to standard error, and the exit status says so.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " PATH"
Config file listing the read-only sources to scan (default
.IR expiry-radar.json ).
.TP
.BI \-format " FORMAT"
Output format:
.BR table ", " json ", " ical ", " prometheus ", " html
(default table).
.TP
.BI \-endpoints " HOSTS"
Comma-separated hosts to probe over TLS, in addition to the config.
.TP
.BI \-domains " DOMAINS"
Comma-separated domains to check via RDAP, in addition to the config.
.TP
.BI \-within " N"
Only report items expiring within N days (0 = everything).
.TP
.BI \-fail\-within " N"
Exit 1 if anything expires within N days (0 = never fail).
.TP
.BI \-min\-priority " P"
Only report items at or above this priority.
.TP
.BI \-out " FILE"
Write to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI \-only " NAMES"
Comma-separated source names to run, instead of every configured source. Names
are matched exactly, so the two carrying a colon are written in full:
.BR tls:endpoint ", " domain:rdap "."
A name that no configured source answers to is an error, not an empty run, and
the message lists what the config did build.
.TP
.BI \-timeout " DURATION"
Overall collection timeout (default 2m).
.TP
.B \-verify\-aws
Run the AWS adapters and report what they did, in a form safe to paste into an
issue (no ARNs, ids or names). This is not a scan.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; nothing breached the
.B \-fail\-within
window.
.TP
.B 1
Something expires within the
.B \-fail\-within
window.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, bad config, or the report could not be written.
.TP
.B 3
Results were produced, but at least one source failed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Credentials are never read from the configuration file. Each source that needs
one takes it from the environment at startup, so nothing secret is written to
disk beside the config. A source is only constructed when the config enables
it, so only the variables for the sources in use are read.
.TP
.B VAULT_ADDR
Vault address, when
.I vault.addr
is not set in the config.
.TP
.B VAULT_TOKEN
Vault token. Needs read and list.
.TP
.B CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
Cloudflare API token, read-scoped.
.TP
.B GITLAB_TOKEN
GitLab personal access token with
.BR read_api .
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
GitHub token. See the project documentation for what GitHub cannot report.
.TP
.B AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET
Client secret for the Entra ID application registration.
.TP
.B GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS
Path to a Google Cloud service-account key file.
.TP
.B OKTA_API_TOKEN
Okta API token.
.TP
.B FASTLY_API_TOKEN
Fastly API token.
.TP
.B HCLOUD_TOKEN
Hetzner Cloud API token.
.TP
.B SCW_SECRET_KEY
Scaleway secret key.
.TP
.B DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN
DigitalOcean personal access token.
.TP
.B NAMECHEAP_API_KEY
Namecheap API key. The Namecheap API also requires a static allowlisted client
IP address.
.TP
.B DNSIMPLE_TOKEN
DNSimple API token.
.TP
.B GANDI_API_KEY
Gandi API key.
.TP
.BR PORKBUN_API_KEY ", " PORKBUN_SECRET_KEY
Porkbun API key and secret.
.TP
.BR GODADDY_API_KEY ", " GODADDY_API_SECRET
GoDaddy API key and secret. GoDaddy gates API access on holding ten or more
domains.
.TP
.B HARBOR_PASSWORD
Harbor password, for the user named in the config.
.TP
.B JFROG_ACCESS_TOKEN
JFrog Artifactory access token.
.TP
.B APP_STORE_CONNECT_KEY_FILE
Path to the App Store Connect
.I .p8
private key, when
.I apple.privateKeyFile
is not set in the config.
.TP
.BR ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_KEY ", " OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY ", " DOCKERHUB_TOKEN
Admin keys for the rotation-policy inventory. These providers state no expiry,
so the deadline reported for them is the configured policy age, not a date the
provider gave.
.PP
AWS uses the standard AWS credential chain and reads no variable of its own.
The
.BR tls:endpoint ", " domain:rdap ", " federation " and " manual
sources need no credential at all.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I expiry-radar.json
Default configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Probe two hosts with no config file at all:
.PP
.RS
.B expiry-radar \-endpoints example.com,api.example.com
.RE
.PP
Fail a CI job if anything expires inside a fortnight:
.PP
.RS
.B expiry-radar \-fail\-within 14
.RE
.PP
Scrape it from Prometheus:
.PP
.RS
.B expiry-radar \-format prometheus \-out /var/lib/node_exporter/expiry.prom
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/expiry-radar
